  "slug": "shipment-exception-authorization-form",
  "title": "Shipment Exception Authorization Form",
  "subtitle": "Shipment Exception: bounds the decision, conditions, and expiry.",
  "description": "Shipment Exception Authorization Form controls shipment, affected unit, route event, service commitment, evidence, and recovery action by tying each Shipment Exception custody, document, or movement decision to the shipper / recovery authority, a stated boundary, and an expiry. The shipment exception coordinator preserves conditions, exceptions, confirmation, and both sides of the handoff.",
  "use_case": "Use Shipment Exception Authorization Form at origin, in-transit node, destination, vehicle, and recovery location. Check applicable Shipment Exception requirements, list the affected quantity, value, document, route, or custody action, and state its limit. Record whether the shipper / recovery authority approves, conditions, holds, or declines the request; obtain renewed consent before changing shipment, affected unit, route event, service commitment, evidence, and recovery action scope.",
  "risk_tier": "B",
  "sections": [
    {
